You can hold the iPhone Duo and set it down in a number of ways, such as partially folded like a book, placed down on a surface, or standing on its edges:<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iphone-duo-poses.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="288" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072201" /><br/>
With the Netflix app, for example, Apple said iPhone Duo users can scroll through a feed of short, vertical movie and TV show clips on the outer display to discover something new to watch, and then open the device to keep watching on the inner display. Apple's screenshot shows the Netflix app on an iPhone Duo in a "seated" pose.<br/>
<br/>
Apple also showed off Amazon's Prime Video app in a "seated" position.<br/>
<br/>
